tap-sync-formula: PENDING

# What this file is
#
# `Formula/keel.rb` no longer exists in this repository (#1023, #990). The tap —
# berkayturanci/homebrew-keel — pulled that exact path every thirty minutes, so
# until it is repointed at the release asset its sync job 404s on a schedule and
# `brew upgrade` stops seeing releases. That is the failure shape of #981,
# arriving from a new direction.
#
# The change the tap needs ships next to this file rather than as a request that
# someone remember it:
#
#     git -C ../homebrew-keel apply /path/to/keel/packaging/homebrew/tap-sync-formula.patch
#     git -C ../homebrew-keel commit -am "ci: sync the formula from keel's release asset"
#     git -C ../homebrew-keel push
#
# Then record the tap commit it produced, replacing PENDING above with its
# 40-character sha:
#
#     echo "tap-sync-formula: $(git -C ../homebrew-keel rev-parse HEAD)" > packaging/homebrew/TAP_REPOINTED
#
# `tests/test_external_promises.py` requires that line offline, and — under
# KEEL_CHECK_EXTERNAL=1, which CI's `external promises` job sets — checks the
# live tap really no longer names the retired path. The offline half is a claim
# in a reviewable form, not proof: nothing offline can read another repository.
# Requiring the sha rather than a non-empty file is what makes the claim
# falsifiable.
#
# Both the marker and its gate are single-use. Delete them once the tap has been
# repointed for a release or two and nobody is tempted to restore the committed
# formula.
